# Credential downloads. PyPI hands recovery codes over as a timestamped file
# that lands in whatever directory the browser saves to, so match the pattern
# rather than one filename. See also .pypirc above.
*Recovery-Codes*
*recovery-codes*
*.recovery-codes.txt

# Working scratch that lives in the repo directory but is not part of the project.
# These were committed by accident in af28d40 and untracked again afterwards.
# Listed by name and anchored with a leading slash rather than globbed as *.txt,
# so real content such as docs/requirements.txt stays tracked.
/Anti text spoofing.docx
/marketing_plan.txt
/metadata.txt
/notes.txt
/table_notes.txt
/temp.py
/unicode.txt
/wheel.txt

# Design notes rather than importable code. Globbed on the stem so the rename from
